      "author_association": "MEMBER",
      "body": "The legacy python tests [appear to run](https://travis-ci.org/neovim/neovim/jobs/475527868#L6419-L6458) in Travis, but that's only because the `has('python')`/`has('python3')` checks are failing, short-circuiting the rest of the tests.\r\n\r\nIf they weren't, then https://github.com/neovim/neovim/blob/38b4ca26b555e5bdca4d672917a85f1bd60297c2/src/nvim/testdir/test_python2.vim#L39 would be failing since pynvim doesn't provide `bindeval()`.\r\n\r\nThe functional tests _are_ [successfully running](https://travis-ci.org/neovim/neovim/jobs/475527868#L5214), so something is different about the environment when running the legacy tests that causes them to not find the Python providers.\r\n\r\n---\r\nI ran into this when preparing the Debian package for 0.3.3, since it _was_ able to successfully execute `has('python')` for the legacy tests.",
